<h2 id="how-fare-works">How the tempo traveller fare is calculated</h2>
<p>A tempo traveller fare from Delhi is usually made up of these parts:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Kilometre charge:</strong> total distance from pick-up in Delhi back to Delhi, multiplied by the per km rate.</li>
    <li><strong>Minimum kilometres per day:</strong> on outstation trips most operators charge a minimum distance per day, even if you drive less (for example on a sightseeing day in Manali).</li>
    <li><strong>Driver allowance:</strong> a daily amount for the driver’s food and stay on multi-day trips.</li>
    <li><strong>Toll and parking:</strong> paid as actuals along the route.</li>
    <li><strong>State permit / entry tax:</strong> charged when the tempo enters another state such as Uttarakhand, Himachal Pradesh or Rajasthan.</li>
    <li><strong>Night charges:</strong> some trips add a charge if the driver drives late at night (with us, ₹500 for driving between 10 PM and 6 AM).</li>
</ul>
<div class="callout note"><i class="fas fa-info-circle"></i><p>Always ask whether your quote is “all-inclusive” or “plus toll, parking, permit and driver allowance”. Two quotes that look far apart can end up costing the same once these are added. Our per km rate already includes toll, state tax and driver allowance; only parking, GST and a ₹500 driver night charge (10 PM – 6 AM) are extra.</p></div>

