<h2 id="local-vs-outstation">Local Delhi NCR hire vs outstation hire</h2>
<p>For <strong>local use within Delhi NCR</strong> (a wedding, an airport transfer, a city tour or an office event), a tempo traveller is normally quoted as a package, for example a set number of hours and kilometres with extra hours and kilometres charged separately. For <strong>outstation trips</strong>, per km pricing with a daily minimum is the norm.</p>
<p>If your plan mixes both, like a morning pick-up from Noida and Gurugram followed by a drive to Agra, tell us every pick-up point in advance so we can include it in the quote.</p>

<h2 id="save-money">7 ways to get the best price on a tempo traveller</h2>
<ol>
    <li><strong>Book early</strong> for long weekends, Diwali, summer holidays and the Char Dham season.</li>
    <li><strong>Choose the right size.</strong> Do not pay for a 20 seater if 12 seats will do. Our <a href="12-16-20-seater-tempo-traveller-which-to-choose.php">12 vs 16 vs 20 seater guide</a> helps you decide.</li>
    <li><strong>Plan your route in one loop</strong> so you are not paying for extra kilometres going back and forth.</li>
    <li><strong>Travel mid-week</strong> when demand on popular routes is lower.</li>
    <li><strong>Ask for a round-trip package</strong> for longer tours such as the <a href="golden-triangle-tour-by-tempo-traveller.php">Golden Triangle</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Get everything in writing</strong>: rate, minimum km, driver allowance, tolls and permits.</li>
    <li><strong>Book directly with the operator</strong>, which avoids middleman commissions.</li>
</ol>

